---

The widget toolkit, its raylib adapter and the Spectrum palettes are
github.com/ha1tch/zenui (zenui, zenui/zenuiraylib, zenui/zxpalette) and
the BDF font reader is github.com/ha1tch/zentools (pkg/bdf): same
author, likewise Apache 2.0. Until 0.27.0 this tree carried its own
copies of the four (pkg/zenui, pkg/zenuiraylib, pkg/zxpalette, pkg/bdf),
which came from github.com/ha1tch/zenimate and grew here.

The Help and About window is zenui's TextModal, which was written here
after zenimate's own helpModal (cmd/zenimate-gui/helpmodal.go, same
author, likewise Apache 2.0) and moved to zenui for its 0.2.0.

pkg/fonts/sinclair.bdf is the ZX Spectrum 48K ROM's own character set;
see pkg/fonts/LICENSE-Sinclair.txt for the Amstrad/Cliff Lawson
permission it carries, the same basis rom/SINCLAIR.txt already
documents for the ROM images in rom/.

github.com/ha1tch/queryfy (same author) validates machines.json,
Apache 2.0.

github.com/ha1tch/blipper (same author), Apache 2.0 -- pkg/nextdisk
imports its fatfs subpackage (a standalone FAT16/FAT32 driver with no
dependency of its own beyond the standard library) to read files off
a FAT disk image, in support of T-33's ZX Spectrum Next boot-chain
work. Nothing else from blipper is used.
